From: Amazing A32 kernel bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/dtc: avoid duplicate yylloc definition on modern hosts

GCC 10 changed the default from -fcommon to -fno-common.  This old DTC lexer
defines yylloc even though the parser also provides the definition, so linking
the host dtc fails with a multiple-definition error.  Keep only the parser
definition and declare it extern in the lexer.

Patch both the flex source and the shipped generated lexer because this vendor
tree builds the shipped file directly.

--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.l
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 extern bool treesource_error;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
@@ -637,7 +637,7 @@
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 extern bool treesource_error;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
